WEBVTT

00:00.890 --> 00:04.020
<b>AUGUST 4, A.D. 2096
STEEPLECHASE
CROSS-COUNTRY COURSE</b>

00:13.650 --> 00:16.410
<b>What on earth is this stringent security?</b>

00:17.950 --> 00:20.240
<b>Is there any spot where I can infiltrate?</b>

00:22.120 --> 00:23.040
<b>Huh?</b>

00:23.750 --> 00:24.920
<b>Is that...</b>

00:25.620 --> 00:27.540
<b>Were you able to find the entrance?</b>

00:27.540 --> 00:30.630
<b>No. It doesn't look like we can sneak in.</b>

00:32.920 --> 00:34.430
<b>Fumiya, Ayako...</b>

00:35.800 --> 00:37.430
<b>Big Bro Tatsuya!</b>

00:38.720 --> 00:42.020
<b>Mr. Tatsuya, please don't scare us like that!</b>

00:42.020 --> 00:43.890
<b>Well, that wasn't my intention.</b>

00:44.190 --> 00:48.020
<b>Then, you shouldn't have spoken
in such a scary way!</b>

00:50.730 --> 00:53.240
<b>Are you two here
to check out the course, too?</b>

00:53.240 --> 00:54.400
<b>Yes.</b>

00:54.400 --> 00:56.910
<b>But security's so tight.</b>

00:56.910 --> 00:58.780
<b>We couldn't get in.</b>

00:59.070 --> 01:01.080
<b>Should we give it one more try?</b>

01:01.490 --> 01:04.710
<b>No. I think we should go back for tonight.</b>

01:05.040 --> 01:05.960
<b>I agree!</b>

01:05.960 --> 01:07.210
<b>- Who's that?
- Who's that?</b>

01:07.790 --> 01:11.670
<b>Like Tatsuya said, it would be better
to withdraw for tonight.</b>

01:12.510 --> 01:15.510
<b>Mr. Tatsuya, by any chance, is that...</b>

01:15.510 --> 01:16.510
<b>Yes.</b>

01:16.510 --> 01:19.430
<b>The ninjutsu-user,
Master Yakumo Kokonoe.</b>

01:20.100 --> 01:22.720
<b>Master, did you find out something?</b>

01:22.720 --> 01:23.560
<b>Nope.</b>

01:24.020 --> 01:26.810
<b>They didn't even have
the course set up yet.</b>

01:26.810 --> 01:28.980
<b>You were able to get onto the course?!</b>

01:30.860 --> 01:33.940
<b>So, what was it like inside?</b>

01:33.940 --> 01:36.280
<b>You did say there was nothing there.</b>

01:36.280 --> 01:37.820
<b>It's just as I said.</b>

01:38.160 --> 01:41.830
<b>Right now, it's still just an ordinary
man-made forest for drills...</b>

01:42.120 --> 01:45.160
<b>with ordinary obstacles set up.</b>

01:45.160 --> 01:48.920
<b>Can we predict where they might
set up the parasite dolls?</b>

01:48.920 --> 01:50.080
<b>No, we can't.</b>

01:50.750 --> 01:53.340
<b>No matter where they're placed,
it wouldn't make much difference.</b>

01:53.340 --> 01:57.260
<b>That's how this place was built.</b>

03:28.600 --> 03:32.730
<b>AUGUST 5, A.D. 2096
FIRST DAY OF THE COMPETITION</b>

03:29.810 --> 03:32.230
<b><i>At last, the time
has come to open...</i></b>

03:32.230 --> 03:37.480
<b><i>the 2096 National Magic High School
Goodwill Tournament of Magic Skills!</i></b>

03:32.730 --> 03:35.230
<b>2096 NATIONAL MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
GOODWILL TOURNAMENT
OF MAGIC SKILLS</b>

03:35.230 --> 03:37.480
<b>ROWER AND GUNNER MEN'S PAIR
ROWER AND GUNNER WOMEN'S PAIR
ICE PILLARS BREAK
MEN'S PAIR PRELIMINARY
ICE PILLARS BREAK
WOMEN'S PAIR PRELIMINARY</b>

03:35.230 --> 03:37.480
<b>AUGUST 5 SCHEDULE</b>

03:37.480 --> 03:40.240
<b>FIRST HIGH SCHOOL</b>

03:40.240 --> 03:41.990
<b>How's the event schedule looking?</b>

03:40.240 --> 03:41.990
<b>AUGUST 5, 2096
OPENING CEREMONY</b>

03:42.280 --> 03:46.370
<b>It seems like there's no conflict
with any of the events I'm in.</b>

03:48.240 --> 03:50.620
<b>All right, I'm heading
over to the Row and Gun course.</b>

03:51.460 --> 03:54.380
<b>I know it's going to be tough,
but good luck.</b>

03:59.000 --> 04:00.510
<b>FIRST HIGH SCHOOL
ROWER: KUMIKO KUNISAKI
GUNNER: EIMI AKECHI</b>

04:17.940 --> 04:19.940
<b>FIRST HIGH SCHOOL
KUMIKO KUNISAKI
EIMI AKECHI</b>

04:31.120 --> 04:33.250
<b>This isn't the traditional way of using it...</b>

04:33.620 --> 04:35.920
<b>but you should master tricks
like this, too.</b>

04:35.920 --> 04:36.750
<b>Right!</b>

04:37.420 --> 04:38.500
<b>It's getting late.</b>

04:38.920 --> 04:40.550
<b>Let's call it a day now.</b>

04:40.550 --> 04:41.380
<b>All right.</b>

04:41.880 --> 04:43.510
<b>Thank you very much!</b>

04:47.260 --> 04:49.350
<b>Well? Could you detect anything?</b>

04:49.890 --> 04:52.850
<b><i>I cannot sense the presence of my kind.</i></b>

04:54.230 --> 04:57.150
<b><i>So, they've been put into hibernation?</i></b>

04:57.150 --> 04:59.150
<b><i>Pretty cautious of them.</i></b>

05:21.590 --> 05:23.010
<b><i>Brother...</i></b>

05:24.050 --> 05:29.010
<b><i>I wonder if Brother is cold.</i></b>

05:33.640 --> 05:35.980
<b><i>Aren't you cold, Brother?</i></b>

05:38.150 --> 05:39.560
<b><i>So cold!</i></b>

05:39.560 --> 05:41.820
<b><i>Oh no! I must warm him up!</i></b>

05:42.150 --> 05:46.280
<b><i>Let's see, at times like these,
we should bring our skin together...</i></b>

05:46.650 --> 05:48.070
<b><i>I guess.</i></b>

05:49.870 --> 05:52.540
<b><i>I can't take off my clothes, but...</i></b>

05:55.830 --> 05:57.080
<b><i>Brother...</i></b>

05:57.460 --> 06:00.040
<b><i>allow me to warm you up!</i></b>

06:11.390 --> 06:13.560
<b>She finally fell asleep, huh?</b>

06:16.430 --> 06:18.480
<b>Good night, Miyuki.</b>

06:24.570 --> 06:26.940
<b>FIRST HIGH SCHOOL</b>

06:24.940 --> 06:26.940
<b>AUGUST 6, A.D. 2096
SECOND DAY OF THE COMPETITION</b>

06:29.990 --> 06:31.950
<b><i>Can we talk for a second?</i></b>

06:32.280 --> 06:35.200
<b><i>Yeah, if it's not for too long.</i></b>

06:36.290 --> 06:38.160
<b>About the Steeplechase Event...</b>

06:38.580 --> 06:42.590
<b>it seems like the Anti-Great Asian Alliance
hardliners of the JDF are involved.</b>

06:43.540 --> 06:46.460
<b>And they're working behind the scenes
of the Nine Schools Competition?</b>

06:47.050 --> 06:50.300
<b>Apparently, Colonel Sakai,
the leader of the hardliners...</b>

06:50.300 --> 06:57.220
<b>wants the magic high school students to bypass the
National Defense Academy and join the JDF directly.</b>

06:57.730 --> 06:59.770
<b>I'm surprised you found out his name.</b>

07:00.190 --> 07:04.020
<b>Colonel Sakai is an old acquaintance of my dad's.</b>

07:04.320 --> 07:06.400
<b>Ichijo, don't tell me that—</b>

07:06.400 --> 07:09.150
<b>No, of course not, Shiba!
Don't get the wrong idea!</b>

07:09.450 --> 07:11.410
<b>It was years ago
that they knew each other!</b>

07:12.110 --> 07:18.330
<b>Four years ago, Colonel Sakai was the top commander
in Sado during the invasion.</b>

07:13.990 --> 07:17.870
<b><i>I panicked for a second, thinking even the Ichijos
were involved in this, but luckily...</i></b>

07:17.870 --> 07:19.500
<b><i>my fears were groundless.</i></b>

07:19.870 --> 07:25.540
<b><i>If the situation gets any more complicated,
I'd have to turn the tables with all my might.</i></b>

07:25.840 --> 07:26.630
<b><i>No.</i></b>

07:27.090 --> 07:30.590
<b><i>Why not just destroy
the Steeplechase course?</i></b>

07:31.430 --> 07:33.760
<b><i>If I did that,
it wouldn't matter what's set up.</i></b>

07:34.390 --> 07:36.310
<b><i>Neither the Kudous' goals...</i></b>

07:36.310 --> 07:38.220
<b><i>nor the JDF's intentions...</i></b>

07:38.220 --> 07:40.180
<b><i>have anything to do with me.</i></b>

07:40.980 --> 07:44.270
<b><i>If I fire a Material Burst
right under the surface...</i></b>

07:44.270 --> 07:47.690
<b><i>it'd be indistinguishable
from an ordinary weapon going off.</i></b>

07:48.110 --> 07:52.700
<b><i>But how to convince Miyuki
and who should I use as my scapegoat?</i></b>

07:53.160 --> 07:57.200
<b><i>Should I set the hardliners up to be the culprits
behind the Steeplechase course blast?</i></b>

07:57.700 --> 08:00.700
<b><i>No, engineering a move like that
in so short a time...</i></b>

08:00.960 --> 08:02.710
<b>Shiba, are you listening?</b>

08:03.790 --> 08:05.710
<b>Yes, I'm listening.</b>

08:06.500 --> 08:08.590
<b>You are? Okay, then.</b>

08:09.760 --> 08:13.550
<b><i>It seems like I'm uncharacteristically wavering
too much between this and that.</i></b>

08:16.350 --> 08:19.220
<b>AUGUST 7, A.D. 2096
THIRD DAY OF THE COMPETITION</b>

08:29.320 --> 08:30.280
<b>Take this!</b>

08:33.650 --> 08:34.740
<b>FIRST HIGH SCHOOL</b>

08:47.670 --> 08:48.090
<b>FIRST HIGH SCHOOL</b>

08:53.510 --> 08:55.840
<b>Shizuku, congratulations on your win!</b>

08:55.840 --> 08:56.930
<b>Ms. Kitayama...</b>

08:57.470 --> 08:59.100
<b>Congratulations!</b>

08:59.100 --> 09:00.430
<b>Thanks.</b>

09:00.720 --> 09:02.310
<b>Now that Shizuku's won...</b>

09:02.810 --> 09:05.560
<b>Shiba's undefeated streak
has been extended.</b>

09:05.900 --> 09:09.820
<b>Right, because all of the players
Shiba was in charge of have won!</b>

09:10.150 --> 09:14.530
<b>You win, too, Miyuki, and extend
Mr. Tatsuya's streak even more.</b>

09:14.530 --> 09:16.570
<b>Yes, of course.</b>

09:16.820 --> 09:17.950
<b><i>Master...</i></b>

09:17.950 --> 09:21.580
<b><i>I've detected signs of my kind.
There are 16 of them.</i></b>

09:22.870 --> 09:24.080
<b>Mr. Tatsuya?</b>

09:24.500 --> 09:27.920
<b>It looks like the machine's having
some issues. I'm going to go check on it.</b>

09:32.380 --> 09:34.590
<b>Are they still giving off signs?</b>

09:34.590 --> 09:37.340
<b><i>They all vanished at once a moment ago.</i></b>

09:37.640 --> 09:40.010
<b><i>I believe they're in hibernation mode now.</i></b>

09:40.300 --> 09:41.470
<b>I see.</b>

09:42.180 --> 09:44.770
<b><i>Being so indecisive won't get me anywhere.</i></b>

09:45.140 --> 09:47.100
<b><i>I'm just going to set it up from my side!</i></b>

09:55.400 --> 09:56.650
<b>Brother...</b>

09:57.150 --> 09:59.870
<b>You're about to head out, aren't you?</b>

10:00.160 --> 10:01.200
<b>Yes.</b>

10:01.200 --> 10:05.250
<b>That's what I thought,
so I had everyone leave.</b>

10:06.580 --> 10:07.750
<b>Brother...</b>

10:08.460 --> 10:10.000
<b>Please don't go.</b>

10:11.290 --> 10:13.710
<b>What's going on, Miyuki?</b>

10:14.000 --> 10:19.050
<b>Is it really necessary for you
to go to the enemy right now, Brother?</b>

10:19.550 --> 10:21.510
<b>I just don't see it that way.</b>

10:21.850 --> 10:24.680
<b>Pixie's detected the enemy's location.</b>

10:24.680 --> 10:26.730
<b>I finally have a clue to work with.</b>

10:27.020 --> 10:29.190
<b>What I'd like to ask is...</b>

10:29.190 --> 10:35.190
<b>why you must mobilize to stop
the Kudous' experiment in advance.</b>

10:36.240 --> 10:39.070
<b>This may be selfishness on my part.</b>

10:39.450 --> 10:43.490
<b>Such shameless thoughts
might be occurring to me...</b>

10:43.490 --> 10:47.330
<b>because I haven't been of any use
to you this time.</b>

10:48.120 --> 10:50.420
<b>I'm ready to be reprimanded.</b>

10:50.420 --> 10:52.540
<b>But Brother...</b>

10:52.540 --> 10:55.340
<b>please hear me out first!</b>

10:55.630 --> 11:01.140
<b>There are no grounds whatsoever for you
to be blamed for the Kudous' experiment.</b>

11:01.640 --> 11:07.270
<b>At the same time, there's no reason for you
to assume responsibility for every player...</b>

11:07.270 --> 11:11.100
<b>taking part in the Steeplechase
Cross-country Event.</b>

11:12.480 --> 11:14.020
<b>Brother...</b>

11:14.020 --> 11:16.980
<b>I'm going to speak selfishly now.</b>

11:16.980 --> 11:19.490
<b>I'm about to say
something extremely shameful.</b>

11:20.280 --> 11:24.660
<b>All you have to do, Brother, is protect me!</b>

11:25.030 --> 11:29.500
<b>The only person you need
to be responsible for is me alone!</b>

11:30.460 --> 11:35.880
<b>You don't have to look out for the students
of First High and other schools!</b>

11:37.800 --> 11:41.380
<b>It's all right not to do anything
about the parasite dolls!</b>

11:41.380 --> 11:45.930
<b>Those things can be destroyed
on the day of the experiment!</b>

11:45.930 --> 11:47.890
<b>After all the events have concluded...</b>

11:47.890 --> 11:50.180
<b>I'll dispose of the released main bodies...</b>

11:50.180 --> 11:52.390
<b>in one fell swoop!</b>

11:54.480 --> 11:56.650
<b>If you still insist on going anyway...</b>

11:56.650 --> 12:00.280
<b>then with all due respect, I'll stop you
with every ounce of strength I have!</b>

12:02.820 --> 12:04.200
<b>Stop it, Miyuki!</b>

12:04.200 --> 12:07.330
<b>Don't tell me you'd actually seal my Eyes!</b>

12:07.330 --> 12:10.750
<b>If you do that, you'll end up
being unable to use magic yourself!</b>

12:10.750 --> 12:11.870
<b>I don't care!</b>

12:12.250 --> 12:15.420
<b>It's better than having you overdo it
any more than you already have!</b>

12:15.750 --> 12:17.000
<b>Brother!</b>

12:17.000 --> 12:21.840
<b>Brother, do you even know how much
you've been pushing yourself over and over?</b>

12:22.300 --> 12:25.850
<b>Adjusting the players' CADs
from dawn to dusk...</b>

12:25.850 --> 12:29.470
<b>being consulted by the other tech staff members
after all the matches...</b>

12:29.470 --> 12:33.770
<b>then training the underclassmen until late at night
while you prep for the next day...</b>

12:33.770 --> 12:37.230
<b>And on top of that, you're taking on
the Kudous and the JDF!</b>

12:38.020 --> 12:41.740
<b>Even you won't hold up under all that, Brother!</b>

12:42.110 --> 12:43.780
<b>You're going to...</b>

12:43.780 --> 12:45.610
<b>break!</b>

12:57.380 --> 12:58.380
<b>Miyuki...</b>

12:58.790 --> 13:01.010
<b>You're absolutely right.</b>

13:02.050 --> 13:03.630
<b>I was wrong.</b>

13:05.470 --> 13:07.550
<b>It's just as you say.</b>

13:07.550 --> 13:10.720
<b>You're the only one
I should be protecting.</b>

13:10.720 --> 13:15.140
<b>As long as you were protected,
nothing else should've mattered.</b>

13:15.730 --> 13:19.520
<b>Having you here with me is enough.</b>

13:22.070 --> 13:23.650
<b>Brother...</b>

13:25.990 --> 13:27.490
<b>Let's go back to our room.</b>

13:32.240 --> 13:33.950
<b>THE IRREGULAR
AT MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
STEEPLECHASE PART III</b>

13:33.950 --> 13:36.750
<b>FIRST HIGH SCHOOL</b>

13:34.870 --> 13:36.750
<b>AUGUST 8, A.D. 2096
FOURTH DAY OF THE COMPETITION</b>

13:37.830 --> 13:38.960
<b>Shiba...</b>

13:38.960 --> 13:41.130
<b>It looks like you're in great shape today.</b>

13:41.630 --> 13:42.760
<b>You think so?</b>

13:42.760 --> 13:47.640
<b>Yes. Until yesterday, it seemed to me
like you weren't able to focus 100 percent.</b>

13:47.970 --> 13:50.640
<b>But today you look refreshed.
I can sense your drive.</b>

13:52.600 --> 13:56.020
<b>Shiba, we're going to keep this up
and really get fired up!</b>

14:00.650 --> 14:02.780
<b>AUGUST 9, A.D. 2096
FIFTH DAY OF THE COMPETITION</b>

14:06.360 --> 14:08.280
<b>What do you think?</b>

14:08.660 --> 14:10.530
<b>AUGUST 10, A.D. 2096
SIXTH DAY OF THE COMPETITION</b>

14:14.080 --> 14:17.410
<b>I dedicate this victory to you, Ms. Miyuki!</b>

14:19.670 --> 14:22.670
<b>FOURTH HIGH SCHOOL
FIRST HIGH SCHOOL
THIRD HIGH SCHOOL</b>

14:20.040 --> 14:22.670
<b>AUGUST 11, A.D. 2096
SEVENTH DAY
OF THE COMPETITION</b>

14:32.600 --> 14:34.680
<b>Victory is mine!</b>

14:34.810 --> 14:37.430
<b>AUGUST 12, A.D. 2096
EIGHTH DAY OF THE COMPETITION</b>

14:49.070 --> 14:50.280
<b>Hey, not bad!</b>

14:50.610 --> 14:51.570
<b>Still...</b>

15:03.590 --> 15:04.960
<b>AUGUST 13, A.D. 2096
NINTH DAY OF THE COMPETITION</b>

15:13.300 --> 15:14.930
<b>FIRST HIGH SCHOOL</b>

15:15.310 --> 15:17.520
<b><i>Mr. Tatsuya's undefeated streak...</i></b>

15:17.520 --> 15:19.440
<b><i>preserved!</i></b>

15:22.190 --> 15:23.190
<b>How's it going?</b>

15:23.480 --> 15:25.270
<b><i>No traces of them.</i></b>

15:25.270 --> 15:27.860
<b><i>I assume they're still
in hibernation.</i></b>

15:29.070 --> 15:30.740
<b>Tatsuya...</b>

15:30.740 --> 15:33.240
<b>Master, are you here to cool off?</b>

15:33.570 --> 15:36.080
<b>Well, in my case,
I guess you could call it that.</b>

15:36.540 --> 15:40.830
<b>But I think that young lady
is here to talk to you.</b>

15:42.460 --> 15:46.210
<b>Just as I thought, that message
was from you, then, Lieutenant?</b>

15:50.420 --> 15:55.470
<b>I've been really frustrated
and annoyed because of this matter.</b>

15:55.800 --> 15:59.850
<b>After all, my source has been so reluctant
to release any information.</b>

16:00.180 --> 16:02.650
<b>Uh, Tatsuya, about that, see—</b>

16:02.650 --> 16:06.480
<b>But as long as I ignored the intent of those
pulling the strings behind the scenes,</b>

16:06.480 --> 16:09.610
<b>it turned out not to be that complicated.</b>

16:10.150 --> 16:13.280
<b>First, the Anti-Great Asian Alliance hardliners
changed the events...</b>

16:13.280 --> 16:16.490
<b>of the Nine Schools Competition
to more combat-oriented events.</b>

16:17.580 --> 16:23.000
<b>Next, the Kudous planned to use this change
to field-test the parasite dolls.</b>

16:23.580 --> 16:28.130
<b>It was my grandfather who proposed that.
It seems like my uncle was against it at first.</b>

16:28.460 --> 16:32.590
<b>Then, was it General Kudou who made the decision
to use the defected magicians?</b>

16:32.930 --> 16:35.720
<b>No, that was my uncle's handiwork.</b>

16:35.720 --> 16:39.890
<b>I heard that someone mediating
for the magicians approached him about it.</b>

16:40.180 --> 16:41.680
<b>Is that right?</b>

16:41.680 --> 16:45.150
<b>Then, let's call that person "X" for now.</b>

16:45.770 --> 16:47.940
<b>X ingratiated himself with the Kudous...</b>

16:47.940 --> 16:50.110
<b>hoping to cause the parasite dolls to go berserk...</b>

16:50.110 --> 16:53.200
<b>which would result in the Nine Schools
Competition players either dying...</b>

16:53.200 --> 16:57.070
<b>or else sustaining grave injuries
that could threaten their futures as magicians.</b>

16:57.580 --> 16:59.790
<b>X's ultimate goal is...</b>

16:59.790 --> 17:04.670
<b>to cut off the supply of promising magicians
who would've helped this country...</b>

17:04.670 --> 17:09.800
<b>and by doing so, to thwart Japan
from expanding its clout.</b>

17:10.090 --> 17:13.300
<b>Yes, that's what we're thinking, too.</b>

17:13.300 --> 17:15.380
<b>That's why I'm here.</b>

17:16.640 --> 17:18.600
<b>What do you mean?</b>

17:19.970 --> 17:26.900
<b>Tatsuya, we'd like to ask you to help us
stop the parasite dolls from going berserk.</b>

17:27.940 --> 17:30.190
<b>Help you, did you say?</b>

17:34.740 --> 17:37.070
<b>The parasite doll performance test...</b>

17:37.070 --> 17:42.540
<b>while unofficial, is a task that the Kudou Family
has been charged with by the JDF.</b>

17:42.540 --> 17:46.460
<b>Should we thwart it, it would lead
to infighting at the JDF...</b>

17:46.460 --> 17:49.420
<b>and personal strife between the military
and the Ten Master Clans.</b>

17:50.130 --> 17:54.050
<b>Are you telling me to become
an illegal saboteur?</b>

17:54.590 --> 17:57.800
<b>I wouldn't blame you
for drawing that inference.</b>

18:05.810 --> 18:06.810
<b>It's fine with me.</b>

18:07.650 --> 18:10.310
<b>Thank you, Tatsuya.</b>

18:12.610 --> 18:15.240
<b>All right then, I'll be going now.</b>

18:15.240 --> 18:19.780
<b>I'm going to see this young lady off.
You know, just in case.</b>

18:19.780 --> 18:22.200
<b>Yes, if you could do that.</b>

18:27.620 --> 18:29.040
<b>Young lady...</b>

18:29.040 --> 18:33.460
<b>Those parasite dolls aren't really
going to spin out of control, are they?</b>

18:34.090 --> 18:35.880
<b>What do you mean by that?</b>

18:36.470 --> 18:41.430
<b>Esoteric Buddhism also has magic
for using dolls as puppets.</b>

18:41.430 --> 18:45.890
<b>I asked an expert about it the other day
when I went to the head temple.</b>

18:45.890 --> 18:48.600
<b>Apparently, no matter who the magician is,
he never forgets...</b>

18:48.600 --> 18:52.310
<b>what he's defined as the object
of his protection or destruction.</b>

18:52.310 --> 18:57.780
<b>And if the puppet breaks that rule,
he'll punish it and seal it away.</b>

18:57.780 --> 19:03.620
<b>He said everything up to that Sealing Spell
was one single Controlling Spell.</b>

19:09.670 --> 19:13.840
<b>The parasite dolls have the same kind
of spell installed, don't they?</b>

19:14.420 --> 19:19.090
<b>Otherwise, they couldn't be used
as autonomous military weapons.</b>

19:20.090 --> 19:22.090
<b>You're absolutely correct.</b>

19:22.390 --> 19:27.270
<b>Even if the tacticians try to get the parasite dolls
to attack these high school students,</b>

19:27.270 --> 19:30.310
<b>the original spell wouldn't allow it.</b>

19:30.310 --> 19:32.730
<b>The instant they started to go berserk,</b>

19:32.730 --> 19:38.030
<b>the Controlling Spell would switch
to a Sealing Spell and seal off the parasite.</b>

19:38.030 --> 19:39.860
<b>That's what I've heard.</b>

19:43.370 --> 19:46.870
<b>So, that's the story, but tell me,
did you know about this?</b>

19:47.330 --> 19:52.080
<b>That there was no need for Tatsuya
to put himself in danger?</b>

19:52.080 --> 19:53.750
<b>Kazama?</b>

19:54.790 --> 19:55.960
<b>No.</b>

19:55.960 --> 19:57.760
<b>I didn't know.</b>

19:58.090 --> 20:01.300
<b>You didn't tell Tatsuya either, Master.</b>

20:01.630 --> 20:04.010
<b>Why didn't you stop him?</b>

20:04.350 --> 20:07.890
<b>Because if I'd stopped him,
there would've been trouble.</b>

20:08.470 --> 20:12.390
<b>What we just discussed
is just a generalization.</b>

20:12.770 --> 20:17.860
<b>This time around, it's possible
that it won't go as planned.</b>

20:17.860 --> 20:19.400
<b>What do you mean?</b>

20:19.990 --> 20:27.990
<b>The parasites came from a different dimension
than this world, drawn by powerful, pure thoughts.</b>

20:28.790 --> 20:33.170
<b>They'll fuse with the owners
of those thoughts and be activated.</b>

20:33.540 --> 20:34.420
<b>Don't tell me...</b>

20:35.130 --> 20:37.170
<b>Strong, pure thoughts.</b>

20:37.630 --> 20:41.220
<b>You couldn't find a place
bursting with more of those...</b>

20:41.220 --> 20:44.720
<b>than on the final day of the Nine Schools
Competition when victory is at stake, right?</b>

20:45.090 --> 20:49.220
<b>You mean the spell restraining
the parasite dolls will malfunction?</b>

20:50.310 --> 20:52.350
<b>I don't know about that.</b>

20:52.350 --> 20:57.190
<b>But neither can I say with conviction
that they won't go berserk.</b>

20:58.150 --> 21:04.860
<b>So, I think it was the right call
to give Tatsuya that combat suit.</b>

21:05.280 --> 21:08.830
<b>Your arbitrary decision to have Tatsuya
annihilate the parasite dolls...</b>

21:08.830 --> 21:14.870
<b>causing them to give up on their foolish plot
to use them as specters for warfare...</b>

21:14.870 --> 21:17.250
<b>should probably work out in the end, too.</b>

21:17.880 --> 21:21.880
<b>That's why I'm going to keep this to myself.</b>

21:22.550 --> 21:25.220
<b>In return, I'd like you to tell me something.</b>

21:25.550 --> 21:26.970
<b>What would that be?</b>

21:26.970 --> 21:32.350
<b>Who was it that sent the magicians
from the Continent to the Kudous?</b>

21:32.770 --> 21:36.650
<b>A young man from the Chinatown
in Yokohama named Gongjin Zhou.</b>

21:36.650 --> 21:39.770
<b>Hmm, Gongjin Zhou, huh?</b>

21:39.770 --> 21:42.150
<b>That's a name that keeps coming up lately.</b>

21:42.150 --> 21:44.570
<b>Master, do you know him?</b>

21:44.570 --> 21:48.820
<b>All right, I've learned what I wanted to know,
so I'll be taking off now.</b>

21:48.820 --> 21:53.540
<b>Like I promised, I'll keep my mouth shut
about the cover-up and your backroom dealings.</b>

21:58.130 --> 21:59.340
<b>Captain, um—</b>

21:59.340 --> 22:00.540
<b>Let's go, Lieutenant.</b>

22:01.340 --> 22:03.800
<b>I don't want Tatsuya to see us like this.</b>

23:36.310 --> 23:39.940
<b>THE IRREGULAR
AT MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
STEEPLECHASE PART IV</b>
